CAT = "s24Research"; SEG = "RES"
Q = [
('A member was an underwriter in a company\'s IPO. Under Rule 2241 it may not publish research on the company for how long after the IPO date?',
 '10 days', ['3 days', '25 days', '40 days'],
 'Rule 2241(b)(2)(I)(i) requires a quiet period of at least 10 days after the IPO date for a member that acted as an underwriter or dealer in the IPO.'),
('A member acted as co-manager of a secondary offering. Rule 2241 bars it from publishing research on the issuer for how long after the offering date?',
 '3 days', ['10 days', '15 days', '30 days'],
 'Rule 2241(b)(2)(I)(ii) sets a quiet period of at least three days after a secondary offering for a member that acted as a manager or co-manager.'),
('Rule 2241\'s post-offering quiet periods do not apply when the issuer is:',
 'An emerging growth company', ['Listed on a national exchange', 'A foreign private issuer', 'A bank holding company'],
 'Rule 2241(b)(2)(I) exempts offerings of emerging growth company securities, consistent with the JOBS Act, from the quiet periods after IPOs and secondary offerings.'),
('Under Rule 2241, a research analyst may not:',
 'Take part in efforts to win investment banking business, such as pitch meetings', ['Talk with sales staff about a published report', 'Attend an industry conference', 'Meet with company management for facts'],
 'Rule 2241(b)(2)(L)(i) prohibits research analysts from participating in efforts to solicit investment banking business, including pitches. A limited exception lets analysts attend emerging growth company IPO pitches without soliciting.'),
('During a public offering, Rule 2241 bars research analysts from:',
 'Participating in road shows', ['Updating models for other companies', 'Reading the issuer\'s public filings', 'Answering investors\' questions after the offering'],
 'Rule 2241(b)(2)(L)(ii) prohibits research analysts from participating in road shows and other marketing on behalf of an issuer related to an investment banking services transaction.'),
('Before publication, a firm may send the subject company parts of a draft research report to check facts, but only if:',
 'The parts omit the summary, rating and price target and a full draft goes to legal or compliance', ['The company agrees in writing to approve the rating', 'The analyst\'s supervisor signs each page', 'The report has already been sent to customers'],
 'Rule 2241.05 allows sharing sections of a draft for factual review only if they exclude the research summary, rating and price target, and a complete draft is first given to legal or compliance; any later rating change needs written justification and approval.'),
('A research report must disclose if the member or its affiliates beneficially own at least what share of a class of the subject company\'s common equity?',
 '1%', ['5%', '10%', '25%'],
 'Rule 2241(c)(4)(F) requires disclosure if the member or its affiliates beneficially own 1 percent or more of any class of common equity of the subject company, measured as of the end of the prior month.'),
('A research report must disclose whether the member expects to receive or intends to seek investment banking compensation from the subject company within the next:',
 'Three months', ['One month', '12 months', 'Two years'],
 'Rule 2241(c)(4)(C) requires disclosure of investment banking compensation received in the past 12 months and expected to be received or sought in the next three months.'),
('Under Rule 2241, a research analyst\'s appearance counts as a public appearance when the analyst speaks at a seminar or on a call before at least:',
 '15 persons', ['5 persons', '25 persons', '100 persons'],
 'Rule 2241(a)(7) defines a public appearance as participation in a conference call, seminar, forum or other public speaking activity before 15 or more persons or before one or more representatives of the media.'),
('A firm decides to stop covering a company in its research. Rule 2241 requires it to:',
 'Notify customers promptly and give a final report or explain why there is none', ['Get the company\'s consent to end coverage', 'Wait one year before ending coverage', 'Delete all earlier reports from its website'],
 'Rule 2241(f) requires a member that terminates coverage to notify its customers promptly, using the same means of distribution, with a final report including a final rating or recommendation, or an explanation if one is impractical.'),
('Under Rule 2241, a research analyst\'s pay may NOT be based on:',
 'Specific investment banking transactions', ['The quality and accuracy of research', 'Feedback from the firm\'s customers', 'Overall productivity of the analyst'],
 'Rule 2241(b)(2) bars compensation based on specific investment banking services transactions or contributions to them, and requires a committee without investment banking representatives to review analyst pay at least annually.'),
('Before a firm sends customers research written by an unaffiliated third party that it did not independently select, Rule 2241(h) requires:',
 'Approval by a registered principal or supervisory analyst', ['FINRA to review the report first', 'Each customer to agree to receive it', 'The third party to register with FINRA'],
 'Rule 2241(h)(1) requires a registered principal or supervisory analyst to review and approve third-party research distributed by the member, except independent third-party research that the member does not review or select.'),
('Under SEC Regulation AC, a research report must include a certification by the analyst that:',
 'The views expressed reflect the analyst\'s personal views', ['The firm guarantees the price target', 'The issuer approved the report\'s content', 'No one at the firm owns the stock'],
 'Regulation AC requires a clear certification that the views accurately reflect the analyst\'s personal views and a statement whether any part of the analyst\'s pay was related to the specific recommendations or views.'),
('Under FINRA Rule 2242, debt research distributed only to eligible institutional investors:',
 'Is exempt from many of the rule\'s provisions, with disclosure that it is meant for institutions', ['Is never allowed under FINRA rules', 'Must be pre-approved by FINRA', 'Is exempt from every FINRA rule'],
 'Rule 2242 provides an institutional investor exemption: debt research given only to eligible institutional investors is exempt from most of the rule\'s requirements, though core protections, such as barring retaliation and promises of favorable research, still apply.'),
('A firm\'s compliance department places a company on its confidential watch list because the bankers are working on a deal. The watch list is used to:',
 'Monitor trading in the stock without restricting it publicly', ['Ban all solicited trades in the stock', 'Tell customers a deal is coming', 'Stop the research department from publishing at all'],
 'A watch list is confidential and lets compliance monitor employee and proprietary trading for misuse of material non-public information. A restricted list, once a deal is public, limits solicitation, trading and research.'),
('Rule 2241\'s exemption from many research separation requirements is available to a member that, over the past three years, averaged no more than 10 managed or co-managed investment banking deals a year and earned no more than:',
 '$5 million a year in gross investment banking revenue from them', ['$1 million a year in total revenue', '$50 million a year in total assets', '$25 million a year in commissions'],
 'Rule 2241(i) exempts members that over the previous three years averaged 10 or fewer investment banking transactions as manager or co-manager a year and generated $5 million or less a year in gross investment banking revenue from them.'),
]
